{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":81018,"duration_api_ms":103994,"num_turns":13,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4e02043c-0935-4740-919a-d0cfd53b20e8","total_cost_usd":0.49548945,"usage":{"input_tokens":1351,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31679,"cache_read_input_tokens":306286,"output_tokens":2696,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31679,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":68,"outputTokens":4096,"cacheReadInputTokens":213797,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22616,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0701977,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1351,"outputTokens":2696,"cacheReadInputTokens":306286,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31679,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.42529175,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed all three amendments against the actual codebase state. fr-5-b737f90d is a minor cleanup suggestion — the function is a no-op identity function, so the unused _unit param is harmless. fr-5-60828312 is factually wrong — the code compiles fine, all references use canonical names. fr-5-b7289131 identifies a real semantic issue: serde aliases on ProcessParams accept legacy _mg keys without the /20 volume normalization, so direct deserialization bypassing parse_process_params_preset yields incorrect values.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-b737f90d","decision":"reject","rationale":"The cited function `normalize_process_param_for_provenance` is a trivial identity function (returns `value` unchanged) — it performs no normalization at all, so the _unit parameter being unused cannot cause a mismatch between stated unit and displayed value. The actual legacy normalization happens earlier in `normalize_legacy_process_params_preset` via `legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l`. Removing the unused parameter would be harmless cleanup but is not a correctness issue."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-60828312","decision":"reject","rationale":"Factually incorrect. The codebase compiles cleanly — `cargo check -p tank_data` succeeds with no errors. All field references at the cited lines (presets.rs:1565-1579, presets.rs:2339, tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:367-386) already use the canonical `*_mg_c_per_l` / `*_mg_n_per_l` / `*_mg_per_l` names. The rename has been completed consistently across the codebase."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-b7289131","decision":"accept","rationale":"The core issue is real: `ProcessParams` (tank_core/src/types/process.rs:59-112) has `serde(alias = \"aob_k_tan_mg\")` etc. on fields like `aob_k_tan_mg_n_per_l`. Direct serde deserialization of a legacy payload with `aob_k_tan_mg = 0.5` into this struct accepts the value as-is (0.5 mg N/L), whereas the intended legacy semantics require dividing by 20 (yielding 0.025 mg N/L). The TOML preset loader (`parse_process_params_preset`) correctly applies `legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l` (value / 20.0), but any codepath that deserializes directly via serde — including the `ProcessParamsPreset` struct aliases at presets.rs:763-801 — bypasses this conversion. The aliases create a false impression that legacy keys are handled when they're actually given wrong semantics. A proper migration/conversion layer should be the only path for legacy keys."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6c66f738-bf84-47af-901b-bc7eda888a7f"}
